{"content":[{"c":["JESHURUN*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Poetical name for Israel, possibly derived from the Hebrew root meaning “upright,” but according to many scholars a diminutive of Israel. The name Jeshurun is mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.32.15","r":"Deut.32.15","rawR":"Deut.32.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.32.15","value":"Deut.32.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deuteronomy 32:15"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.33.5,26","r":"Deut.33.5,26","rawR":"Deut.33.5,26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.33.5,26","value":"Deut.33.5,26"}],"t":"ref","v":"33:5, 26"}," (see ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg). In the Septuagint, the word is not translated as a proper name but as an adjective, “beloved.” In ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.44.2","r":"Isa.44.2","rawR":"Isa.44.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.44.2","value":"Isa.44.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isaiah 44:2"}," Jacob is described as “Israel, my chosen one” (with mg note saying “Jeshurun,” see ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), thus linking the name with the idea of election. In ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.33.5","r":"Deut.33.5","rawR":"Deut.33.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.33.5","value":"Deut.33.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deuteronomy 33:5"}," Israel is reminded that “the ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"divine-name","t":"span"}," became king in Jeshurun” (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), and in verse ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.33.26","r":"Deut.33.26","rawR":"Deut.33.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.33.26","value":"Deut.33.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"26"}," it is told that there is none like God. If we follow the Septuagint, there is a link with the term “beloved” used of Christ (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.3.17","r":"Matt.3.17","rawR":"Matt.3.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.3.17","value":"Matt.3.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 3:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.1.11","r":"Mark.1.11","rawR":"Mark.1.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.1.11","value":"Mark.1.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 1:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Eph.1.6","r":"Eph.1.6","rawR":"Eph.1.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eph.1.6","value":"Eph.1.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eph 1:6"},") and of the church (",{"href":"?bref=Col.3.12","r":"Col.3.12","rawR":"Col.3.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Col.3.12","value":"Col.3.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Col 3:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Thes.1.4","r":"1Thes.1.4","rawR":"1Thes.1.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Thes.1.4","value":"1Thes.1.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 1:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Thes.2.13","r":"2Thes.2.13","rawR":"2Thes.2.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Thes.2.13","value":"2Thes.2.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Thes 2:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jude.1.1","r":"Jude.1.1","rawR":"Jude.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jude.1.1","value":"Jude.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jude 1:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Jeshurun","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Deuteronomy 32:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.32.15","rawQueryValue":"Deut.32.15","sourceRefExact":"Deut.32.15"},{"anchorText":"33:5, 26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.33.5,26","rawQueryValue":"Deut.33.5,26","sourceRefExact":"Deut.33.5,26"},{"anchorText":"Isaiah 44:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.44.2","rawQueryValue":"Isa.44.2","sourceRefExact":"Isa.44.2"},{"anchorText":"Deuteronomy 33:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.33.5","rawQueryValue":"Deut.33.5","sourceRefExact":"Deut.33.5"},{"anchorText":"26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.33.26","rawQueryValue":"Deut.33.26","sourceRefExact":"Deut.33.26"},{"anchorText":"Mt 3:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.3.17","rawQueryValue":"Matt.3.17","sourceRefExact":"Matt.3.17"},{"anchorText":"Mk 1:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.1.11","rawQueryValue":"Mark.1.11","sourceRefExact":"Mark.1.11"},{"anchorText":"Eph 1:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Eph.1.6","rawQueryValue":"Eph.1.6","sourceRefExact":"Eph.1.6"},{"anchorText":"Col 3:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Col.3.12","rawQueryValue":"Col.3.12","sourceRefExact":"Col.3.12"},{"anchorText":"1 Thes 1:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Thes.1.4","rawQueryValue":"1Thes.1.4","sourceRefExact":"1Thes.1.4"},{"anchorText":"2 Thes 2:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Thes.2.13","rawQueryValue":"2Thes.2.13","sourceRefExact":"2Thes.2.13"},{"anchorText":"Jude 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jude.1.1","rawQueryValue":"Jude.1.1","sourceRefExact":"Jude.1.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ced0bd9a286372a1e2817a14f83c78d6ad7926365b359f6af566acc47bff6bf3","sourceItemName":"Jeshurun","sourceItemOrder":217,"sourceMember":"Articles/J.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Jeshurun","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Jeshurun*","title":"Jeshurun*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}